TALLY_FINAL_MESSAGE={"verdict":"blocked","diagnosis":"Failed the ownership gate conflict-domains a second time with an empty lane, and the two-attempt cap is now exhausted: HEAD is still the prepared base 71f2beba0ecd7358eda99e574e078d081f55bbfa, `git status --porcelain` (including ignored) is empty, the captured patch is empty, neither scripts/make-proxy.sh nor scripts/run-proxy.sh exists on disk, and no artifact of the attempt survives anywhere in the worktree. The driver's `agent produced no commit relative to the prepared base` is the operative failure; the accompanying result-schema-mismatch / result-projection-timeout (finalMessage not projected within 10000 ms, exitEvidencePassed false) is the downstream symptom of the worker exiting without a projected final result, identical in shape to attempt 1, so it is a reproducible task-shape failure rather than a one-off machinery fault and does not warrant spending machinery-retry budget. Attempt 1's retry steering already told the worker exactly what to author and to commit before returning; repeating it a third time is not available and, on the evidence, would not change the outcome. The out-of-task cause that blocks this lane is a contradiction between the task's own deliverables and its binding write boundary: the goal requires run-proxy.sh to write results/receipts/proxy.json and deliveredBehaviors require the first light actually to execute on the GPU, but results/receipts/ is outside conflictDomains [\"scripts/make-proxy.sh\",\"scripts/run-proxy.sh\",\"tests\"] and is not gitignored, so executing the script deposits an untracked results/receipts/proxy.json in the lane that can neither be committed (it would fail conflict-domains) nor left behind (it dirties the worktree the ownership stage validates). Authorized steering comment 7 compounds this by explicitly instructing the worker to `git add` results/receipts/proxy.json — following ratified steering would itself trip conflict-domains. The sibling precedent confirms the grant is the operator's to make: container-recipe committed results/receipts/build.json in c1363cb, and scripts/run-smoke.sh (the cited style reference) writes results/receipts/smoke.json into the repo the same way. Additionally, the authoring work that the single acceptance criterion checks (bash -n plus a grep for the receipt path) is cheap, while the goal drags in a full container build, synthetic-checkpoint construction under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy, and a live single-node serve with first-light assertions; that live execution is what consumes the worker session before it commits, and it belongs to the cp-proxy checkpoint, not to this implementation task. The serve-side technical questions are already settled and need no further investigation: pass --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes, keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6, do not use --skip-mm-profiling, and disregard the superseded VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY steer since the host logs integrated_gpu=False. Operator action: grant results/receipts/proxy.json to this task's write boundary and re-scope the task to authoring plus committing the two scripts, leaving the live first light to cp-proxy.","proposal":{"kind":"amendment-task","paths":["scripts/make-proxy.sh","scripts/run-proxy.sh","tests","results/receipts/proxy.json"],"goal":"Re-scope proxy-tooling to authoring and committing the two scripts, and widen its write boundary to include the receipt the scripts produce. Deliverables: (1) scripts/make-proxy.sh, in the style of scripts/run-smoke.sh, runs inside the flashnext:dev container and builds the synthetic checkpoint under /var/tmp/flashnext-proxy — same architecture identifier as the workload, a handful of layers, 8 experts in block-FP8 with weight_block_size 128 by 128, and a small lookup table using the shard tensor name the mmap path expects — reusing the fork's tests/models/ scaffolding inside the fork checkout instead of inventing generators, and detecting an existing checkpoint so a rebuild is skipped. (2) scripts/run-proxy.sh serves that checkpoint single-node from the container with VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1 and eager execution, requests one greedy completion, asserts finite logits via the API, shuts the server down cleanly, and writes results/receipts/proxy.json, recording the serve env choices in the receipt data so cp-proxy and the later TP=2 serve reproduce them. The serve command must carry --limit-mm-per-prompt with image and video set to 0 (JSON quoted for the shell) so profile_run skips the vision-encoder pass that allocated 274877906944 bytes; keep gpu_memory_utilization at 0.6; do not use --skip-mm-profiling; do not set VLLM_ROCM_APU_UNIFIED_MEMORY, since the host logs integrated_gpu=False and that steer was superseded. PYTORCH_HIP_ALLOC_CONF=expandable_segments:True is optional. (3) Any script-level test coverage lives under tests/. Explicitly out of scope for this task: performing the live GPU first light. The scripts must be authored, syntax-clean, and committed on the assigned branch without requiring a serve run; cp-proxy owns executing run-proxy.sh and producing the real results/receipts/proxy.json. Granting results/receipts/proxy.json to the write boundary matches the container-recipe precedent (results/receipts/build.json committed in c1363cb) and makes authorized steering comment 7 executable instead of self-defeating, and it lets a receipt produced by an opportunistic local run be committed rather than dirtying the lane. Final acts, in order: run every acceptance argv and see it pass, git add only paths inside the widened boundary, git commit, then confirm git status --porcelain is empty before returning a final message.","acceptanceCriteria":[{"id":"proxy-scripts-clean","description":"Both scripts are syntax-clean and reference the receipt path.","argv":["bash","-euc","bash -n scripts/make-proxy.sh scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'results/receipts/proxy.json' scripts/run-proxy.sh"]},{"id":"proxy-serve-flags","description":"run-proxy.sh serves with the mmap PLE path, eager execution, and the text-only multimodal limit that avoids the encoder-profiling OOM.","argv":["bash","-euc","grep -q 'VLLM_PLE_MMAP=1' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -q 'limit-mm-per-prompt' scripts/run-proxy.sh && grep -qE 'enforce.eager|enforce_eager' scripts/run-proxy.sh && ! grep -q 'skip-mm-profiling' scripts/run-proxy.sh"]},{"id":"proxy-checkpoint-layout","description":"make-proxy.sh builds the synthetic checkpoint at the agreed path with block-FP8 128x128 experts and reuses the fork's test scaffolding.","argv":["bash","-euc","grep -q '/var/tmp/flashnext-proxy' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'weight_block_size' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q '128' scripts/make-proxy.sh && grep -q 'tests/models' scripts/make-proxy.sh"]},{"id":"proxy-lane-clean","description":"The lane is fully committed: no uncommitted or untracked files remain after the task's commit.","argv":["bash","-euc","[ -z \"$(git status --porcelain)\" ]"]}],"dependencies":["container-recipe"]}}
